        "Protect credential material and document the risk without exporting hashes unnecessarily.",
        "Paste sample cleartext passwords directly into the main report summary section for review.",
        "Run public online cracking attempts that fall outside the assessment scope."
      ],
      "correctAnswer": 1
    },
    {
      "persona": "Hacktivist",
      "taskMessage": "<b>Imani Vale:</b> There are real people behind those accounts, and none of them agreed to have their credentials copied into a consultant's working folder. Careless handling here would make us precisely the thing we are accusing Northbridge of being.\n\nWe can describe the risk in full without ever holding the material that proves it. Anything else hands leadership a reason to argue with the messenger instead of the finding.",
